==Trivia==
*This was the second set to receive True Forms for all its units.
*All Ubers in this set have small hexagonal shapes surrounding them in their [[True Form|True]]/[[Ultra Form]]s.
*This is the only Uber set to consistently see seasonal variants given to all Ubers present (with the exceptions of [[Wise Empress Nobel (PC Uber Rare Cat)|Wise Empress Nobel]], whose [[Minna de Nyanko Daisensou|source version]] was discontinued before she could be receive one, and Raclesa).
*All of the units from this set reference characters from various mythologies, history and/or popular media:
**[[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Windy]] and [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Thundia]] are modeled after [[wikipedia:Fūjin|Fujin]] and [[wikipedia:Raijin|Raijin]], deities of wind and thunder that are commonly portrayed in a pair.
**[[Kuu (Uber Rare Cat)|Kuu]], [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Kai]] and [[Coppermine (Uber Rare Cat)|Coppermine]] are modeled after (in respective order) [[wikipedia:Sun Wukong|Sun Wukong]], [[wikipedia:Zhu Bajie|Zhu Bajie]] and [[wikipedia:Sha Wujing|Sha Wujing]]; A trio from the novel "[[wikipedia:Journey to the West|Journey to the West]]". Kai's design references that of [[wikia:dragonquest:Alena (Dragon Quest IV)|Alena]], from the ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Quest|Dragon Quest]]'' franchise, while Coppermine's is based on [[Mari Illustrious (Super Rare Cat)|Mari Illustrious]], from ''[[wikipedia:Rebuild of Evangelion|Rebuild of Evangelion]]''.
**[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Kalisa]], is modeled after the vocaloid ''[[wikipedia:Hatsune Miku|Hatsune Miku]]''. Her True Form more specifically resembles [[wikia:vocaloid:Hatsune Miku Append|Miku's Append version]]. Her Evolved Form's name in the Japanese version makes a pun about ''[[wikipedia:Excalibur|Excalibur]]''.
**The [[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Twinstars]] may reference the anime "Onmyoji Two Stars" (Jap. Sousei no Onmyouji), where the 50th series is called "Two Stars. Twins", as well as the second name of the anime "Twin Star Exorcists". Their Japanese names, Shishiru and Komari, along with the text on their mechanical paws reference ''[[wikipedia:Komainu|Komainu]]'', pairs of statues that represent the beginning and end of all things in Japanese Buddhism.
**Wise Empress Nobel may be a reference to [[wikipedia:Alfred Nobel|Alfred Nobel]], a Swedish chemist and inventor who is best known for having established the [[wikipedia:Nobel Prize|Nobel Prizes]].
**[[Jeanne (Legend Rare Cat)|Jeanne]]'s Japanese name, 聖会長ジャンヌダルク (Jeanne d'Arc) is a double reference to [[wikipedia:Joan of Arc|Joan of Arc]] (whose French name is also Jeanne d'Arc) and [[wikia:fategrandorder:Jeanne d'Arc|Jeanne d'Arc]], a character who is similarly based on Joan of Arc.
**[[Myrcia (Uber Rare Cat)|Myrcia]] may reference [[wikia:handoreddo:Claire Harvey|Claire Harvey]] from the light novel series ''[[wikipedia:Hundred (novel series)|Hundred]]''.
**[[Lilin (Uber Rare Cat)|Lilin]]'s name may come from ancient Mesopotamian religion, where ''lilin'' were a form of hostile night spirit that attacked men. It could also originate from Jewish mythology, where ''Lilin'' is used as a term for night spirits as well. Her design is based on that of [[wikipedia:Morrigan Aensland|Morrigan Aensland]], a character from Capcom's ''[[wikipedia:Darkstalkers|Darkstalkers]]'' series.
**[[Terun (Uber Rare Cat)|Terun]] may be a reference to [[wikipedia:Artemis|Artemis]], the Greek goddess of the hunt. Artemis, in turn, was associated with the pre-Greek motif [[wikipedia:Potnia Theron|Potnia Theron]], or Mistress of Animals, which is possibly what Terun's name is based on. Her name could also be a reference to William Tell, who's Japanese name reads as ウィリアム・テル (''Wiriamu <u>Teru</u>'').
**[[Pegasa (Uber Rare Cat)|Pegasa]]'s name may be derived from [[wikipedia:Pegasus|Pegasus]], a winged horse from Greek mythology.
**[[Raclesa (Uber Rare Cat)|Raclesa]] is based on [[wikipedia:Heracles|Heracles]], a hero from Greek mythology who is known for his strength. Her design may also be a reference to [https://ultrakill.wiki.gg/wiki/V1 V1], the player character from the game ''Ultrakill''.
*All units from this set have letters from the Greek alphabet added to their names starting with their Evolved Forms. In alphabetical order, the current ones are:
**α (lowercase Alpha), for Windy.
**β (lowercase Beta), for Thundia.
**γ (lowercase Gamma), for Kuu.
**ζ (lowercase Zeta), for Terun.
**κ (lowercase Kappa), for Coppermine.
**μ (lowercase Mu), for Kai.
**ν (lowercase Nu), for Pegasa
**ξ (lowercase Xi), for Myrcia.
**π (lowercase Pi), for Lilin.
**Σ (uppercase Sigma), for Nobel and Raclesa.
**Φ (uppercase Phi), for the Twinstars.
**χ (lowercase Chi), for Kalisa.
**ψ (lowercase Psi), for Jeanne.
*One of the possible endings for [[Gamatoto Expedition]] log messages is "at the Cyber Academy."

